The round-7 code changes are present, including terminal-state rechecks after suspended socket calls and an async disposer for late connector success. One edge still needs scrutiny: teardown uses the same 64-slot async-operation registry for the socket-close timeout after cancelling existing work, so a saturated registry could prevent the socket close from starting. I’ll verify the shipped tests first, then decide whether this is a blocking, reproducible gap.
